{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination"],"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"title":"Choosing what to record","anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","doc:\/\/JSONValues\/documentation\/JSONValues","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"],"title":"Modules","anchor":"Modules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting"],"title":"Testing","anchor":"Testing"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event is a struct, so the compiler checks its name and every property. A tracker holds back","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the events the user hasn’t consented to, stamps the rest with their session and device, keeps them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on disk and delivers them to your server, sending again when the network or the server fails.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"An-apps-analytics-from-launch","text":"An app’s analytics, from launch","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the events. The tracker rejects an event that breaks a constraint before it is stored or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered, and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value reaches only the destinations that don’t redact it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftUI","import Traffluent","import TrackingPlans","","@Event(name: \"product_added_to_cart\")","struct ProductAddedToCart {","    var productID: String","    @Constrained(.minimum(1), .maximum(10))","    var quantity: Int","}","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build the tracker and start its delivery once, as the app launches:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func startAnalytics(consent: Consent) throws -> Tracker {","    \/\/ The plan and the store each take every @Event in the app, and the library's own.","    let plan = try TrackingPlan()","    \/\/ Records wait on disk until they are delivered, across launches.","    let store = try SegmentStore()","    \/\/ Every event gets its session, and the app, device, OS, locale and network it was tracked on.","    let tracker = Tracker(","        store: store,","        consent: consent,","        enrichers: [.sessions(), .application(), .device(), .operatingSystem(), .locale(), .network()])","","    let collector = HTTPDestination(","        endpoint: collectorURL,","        headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],","        encoder: CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan))","    \/\/ Analytics events only, without their email addresses, 20 at a time or every 30 seconds.","    let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","        to: collector.accepting(.analytics).redactingSensitiveValues())","    Task {","        do {","            try await delivery.execute()  \/\/ for the life of the app","        } catch {","            print(\"Delivery stopped: \\(error)\")","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Every event that won't arrive, and why.","    let rejections = tracker.rejectionReports","    let consentDrops = consent.dropReports","    let storeDrops = store.dropReports","    let collectorDrops = collector.dropReports","    Task {","        await withDiscardingTaskGroup { group in","            group.addTask { for await report in rejections { print(\"Rejected: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in consentDrops { print(\"Not consented: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in storeDrops { print(\"Not stored: \\(report)\") } }","            group.addTask { for await report in collectorDrops { print(\"Not sent: \\(report)\") } }","        }","    }","    return tracker","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then make the tracker the app’s default and hand it to the views, which track through it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@main","struct StoreApp: App {","    let tracker: Tracker","","    init() {","        do {","            \/\/ The user's earlier decisions, which the app saved; undecided categories wait in memory.","            let tracker = try startAnalytics(consent: Consent(savedDecisions))","            \/\/ `Tracker.current` falls back to it where nothing else reaches, such as a detached task.","            try Tracker.bootstrap(tracker)","            self.tracker = tracker","        } catch {","            print(\"Analytics are off: \\(error)\")","            tracker = .noOp","        }","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            CartView()","                .tracker(tracker)","        }","    }","}","","struct CartView: View {","    @Environment(\\.tracker) private var tracker","","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Add to Cart\") {","            tracker.track(ProductAddedToCart(productID: \"canvas-tote\", quantity: 1))","        }","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" imports every module except ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/JSONValues\/documentation\/JSONValues"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence"},{"text":" and the testing modules, which are products of their own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":3},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set it up step by step, from adding the package to testing what you track: ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare events and their constraints: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents"},{"text":"; change one that has shipped:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Track from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit views: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews"},{"type":"text","text":"; let screens, controls and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app’s lifecycle track themselves: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach the tracker from any code, batch records and add context to them: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keep events when the app ends or goes offline before delivering them: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ask for consent and gate events by it: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keep a fraction of events or sessions: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Group events into sessions and stamp them with the app and device: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A session’s key is a UUIDv7, its start time in Unix milliseconds followed by random bits, held in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"memory only.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Export the events’ schemas and catch breaking changes in CI: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Test what your code tracks: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Send to logs, traces, your own server, PostHog, Amplitude, Mixpanel or memory, with values for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one destination alone: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Send to an analytics vendor not yet covered, from a module of your own:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WritingAVendorDestination","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decide what belongs in an event and what stays out of it: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"title":"Traffluent","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"Traffluent","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"title":"Consent Gating","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}]},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"title":"AppKitTracking","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Let AppKit views find their tracker up the responder chain, and track what controls do.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","title":"TracingDestinations","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that adds each tracked event to the span that was active when it was tracked.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","title":"Automatic Tracking","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/GettingStarted":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","title":"Getting Started","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Traffluent to an app, declare its events, deliver them to a server and test what the app tracks."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/gettingstarted","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PrivacyManifests":{"title":"Privacy Manifests","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels.","type":"text"}]},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","title":"EventMacros","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances, name and schema from its struct declaration, and declare the constraints its properties satisfy.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://PropertyJSON/documentation/PropertyJSON":{"title":"PropertyJSON","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON","url":"\/documentation\/propertyjson","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The vendor-neutral pieces a JSON "},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is built from: properties, context, timestamps, identity and batch splitting."}]},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","title":"SwiftUITracking","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give SwiftUI views a tracker through the environment, and track what they do with view modifiers."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking":{"title":"LifecycleTracking","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","url":"\/documentation\/lifecycletracking","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and make the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s records durable as the app leaves the foreground."}]},"doc://JSONValues/documentation/JSONValues":{"title":"JSONValues","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/JSONValues\/documentation\/JSONValues","url":"\/documentation\/jsonvalues","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A JSON value that renders to the same bytes on every platform and Swift release."}]},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","title":"Destinations","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Where tracked events go: the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol, the modifiers that narrow what a destination receives, and the delivery that hands it batches.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinations","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","title":"GRDBPersistence","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"title":"Changing an Event","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChoosingDestinations":{"title":"Choosing Destinations","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Deliver events to your logs, your traces, a server or memory, and decide what each destination may see.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","title":"Traffluent","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Typed analytics events for Swift, delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"title":"MixpanelEncoding","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","title":"Persistence","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"title":"Checksums","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums","url":"\/documentation\/checksums","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The CRC-32 checksum of raw bytes, as zlib, PNG, gzip and Ethernet compute it."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","title":"Identifying People","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"title":"Events","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","url":"\/documentation\/events","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The types every other module shares: the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, the values its properties can hold, and the record a tracker makes of each event."}]},"doc://StandardContext/documentation/StandardContext":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","title":"StandardContext","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale and network connection it was tracked on.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/standardcontext","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","title":"Sampling Events","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"title":"TrackingPlans","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Export every event an app tracks as JSON Schema that people and services outside the app can read, and check each change against the plan committed before it.","type":"text"}]},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding":{"title":"PostHogEncoding","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API."}]},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"title":"Persisting Records","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending.","type":"text"}]},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues":{"